title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-ticklers/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

! About

A tickler is a HyperGSD ''action'' carrying a date field: when the date arrives, the action raises an alert banner linking back to it. Optionally the tickler repeats every N days. This plugin supplies the tickler fields, the inputs for them, and the check that fires due ticklers.

Based on the GSD5 ticklers extension by Roma Hicks (https://gitlab.com/gsd5-tiddlywiki/gsd5-ticklers), reworked for HyperGSD. The GSD5 version corrupts `gsd_tickdate` to `NaNNaNNaN…` when a one-shot tickler fires (GitLab work item 14: an always-true guard makes the field-clearing branch unreachable, and `undefined * 86400000` produces an invalid date that the date widget then chokes on). This implementation never deletes or corrupts the date field: firing is non-destructive, and repeating ticklers advance by whole intervals from the fired date, so a corrupted value can never be written.

! Fields

| Field | Meaning |h
| `gsd_tickler_date` | When the tickler fires, as a TiddlyWiki UTC date string at midnight — the date input carries no time of day. |
| `gsd_tickler_date_history` | Chronological list of every date the tickler has carried — each pick, shift-button press and automatic roll appends the new date; the last entry is always the current date. Not displayed anywhere yet. |
| `gsd_tickler_repeat_days` | Repeat interval in days. Absent, empty, zero or non-numeric means one-shot: the alert fires on the due day and the date is kept. |

A repeating tickler that is marked complete stays complete — its banner still returns on each due date, once per cycle.

! Where the fields appear

* The new-item modal (second column, when the type is action)
* The item attributes panel (second column, on actions) — the tickler date also carries the shift buttons: `+d` `+w` `+m` move the date 1/7/30 days (the arithmetic is day-based, and every shift joins the date history; the buttons are shared tag-list members, also shown on alerts when tagged)
* Every action row in a dashboard list (an always-visible date input in place in the row)
* `GSD/Ticklers` — a dashboard in three sections: ticklers requiring action (due today or overdue), upcoming ticklers, and old ticklers (completed, past-dated) behind a toggle

! The tickler check

The check runs automatically when the wiki loads, at the top of every hour and at local midnight, and only in an open browser session — there is no server-side timer. A tickler whose date is today raises a ''Tickler due'' banner; repeating ticklers advance by whole intervals from the fired date (the weekday is preserved), and a completed repeating tickler still raises one banner on each due date. The date is never removed by firing — an overdue tickler stays in the dashboard until handled — and a tickler missed while the wiki was closed raises a ''Tickler overdue'' banner at the first check after (an overdue one-shot re-raises hourly until handled; a repeating one alerts once per missed occurrence).

! Alerts

A due tickler raises a banner titled //Tickler due// with the due date (the action title itself is not repeated in the banner title — the link below carries it), showing the action title as a link, with a ''Complete'' checkbox and the Alert-tag list shift buttons (`+d`, `+w`) below it. Completing the action dismisses the alert; a shift writes a new due date (the base plus the interval, at midnight) and dismisses the alert. The title link only navigates — a banner closed with the toolbar close button is re-raised at the top of the next hour while the tickler stays due and unrolled (in practice, one-shot ticklers).

The shift buttons are data-only tag-list tiddlers rendered by the shared `$hgsd.tickler-shift` widget: tag `$:/tags/hypergsd/Ticklers/Shift` for the panel set, add `$:/tags/hypergsd/Ticklers/Alert` to also appear on the banner; fields `days`, `label`, `tooltip` (plain text or `<<lingo>>` keys) and an optional `class`. The widget takes `target-tiddler`, `base-date` (panel = stored date, alert = now), `days`, `label`, `tooltip`, `class`, `after-shift-actions` and `lingo-base`, and is equally usable standalone with explicit parameters. This plugin ships +d/+w/+m on the panel (day, week, month tagged Shift) and +d/+w on the banner (day and week carry the Alert tag too); the year member ships withdrawn — its settings entry reads hide, so +y appears in Settings → HyperGSD → Ticklers as an unticked row; tick it to offer +y on the panel. Each set has its own knob there: panel members read `$:/config/hypergsd/Ticklers/Shift/visibility/`, banner members read `$:/config/hypergsd/Ticklers/Alert/visibility/` — a member tagged both answers to both independently.

